#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Restore the reviewed GitHub producer workflows one bounded stage at a time.

Required environment:

* EXPECTED_HOST_SHA: exact Hetzner Phase 3 deployed commit H.
* EXPECTED_PUBLIC_RELEASE_SHA: exact Phase 2 public release commit R.
* PHASE3_FINALIZED_RECEIPT: absolute private Phase 3 finalized receipt.
* PHASE3_PROOF_COMPLETE_RECEIPT: private copy of Phase 3's exact prerequisite.
* PHASE2_V2_HANDOFF_RECEIPT: private canonical Phase 2 H/P/R handoff.
* PRODUCER_RESTORE_EVIDENCE_DIR: absolute, not-yet-existing evidence directory.
* PRODUCER_RESTORE_RECEIPT: absolute, not-yet-existing terminal receipt path.

Optional environment:

* PRODUCER_RESTORE_RESUME_RECEIPT: an exact prior failed-closed receipt.  This
  is the only way a fresh attempt may start from a producer-advanced main.

The helper never opens Railway hourly publication.  It enables and proves the
three reviewed GitHub workflow owners in their fixed order, writes one durable
stage receipt after each proof.  Every failure disables all three owners,
closes the Railway gate, removes only the exact acknowledgement, and writes a
terminal failed-closed receipt that can authorize one reviewed fresh retry.
It never cancels a run it did not create and does not cancel its own run when
the outcome is uncertain.
"""

